      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-146319",
      ":question/problem": "Workers of a small company decided to elect a new board representative. There are $20$ workers, and $55%$ of this worker population will vote for candidate $A$. Let the random variable $X_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$X_{i} = {1, ith member of the population will vote for candidateA; 0, otherwise$\nfor $i = 1, \u2026, 20$. Find $P(X_{2} = 1 \\mid X_{1} = 0)$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
